<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>68.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Gate_Passed</name>
        <label>Gate Passed</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AF_ClosedWonGatePassed__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Opportunity_Delivered</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>After-save on AF_Handover__c (paired with the before-save AF_FL_Handover_UpdateChecklistGate, which computes AF_ClosedWonGatePassed__c): pushes that value up to the parent Opportunity&apos;s AF_HandoverComplete__c, which AF_VR_Opp_ClosedWonGate reads. Does not touch AF_DeliveryConfirmation__c - that field is reserved for the Keyloop/MuleSoft delivery-status sync ( FR2), a different source of truth from the local handover checklist. ALF-RS-12 (LFRDN-342) FR3: when the gate passes, also sets Opportunity.AF_SOStatus__c = &apos;Delivered&apos; - one-way only, never reverts it if the gate later becomes false (e.g. a data fix unchecking a document), since Sales Order status should not silently regress once delivery has been confirmed.

Also sets Opportunity.AF_Handover__c = this Handover&apos;s Id on every save (idempotent). This is a real, previously-undiscovered gap fix: AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate.cls and its before-save mirror AF_FL_Opp_ClosedWonPaymentGate both read the Traffic Form / Customer Sign-Off condition via Opportunity.AF_Handover__c (a lookup FROM the Opportunity TO the Handover) - but nothing in the org ever populated that reverse lookup (only AF_Handover__c.AF_Opportunity__c, the forward lookup, was ever set, e.g. by the Quick Action that creates the Handover). Confirmed via live anonymous Apex against ALFardan DEV (2026-09-16): without this, Closed Won never auto-progresses and the LFRDN-341 handover gate silently evaluates as &quot;no handover found&quot; for every real Opportunity.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Handover Sync Opportunity Gate {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Handover Sync Opportunity Gate</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Opportunity</name>
        <label>Update Opportunity Handover Complete</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Gate_Passed</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_Opportunity__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_HandoverComplete__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_ClosedWonGatePassed__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Handover__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Opportunity_Delivered</name>
        <label>Set Sales Order Status Delivered</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_Opportunity__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_SOStatus__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Delivered</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <runInMode>SystemModeWithoutSharing</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Opportunity</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <object>AF_Handover__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
